   "status": "knowledge",
   "notes": "Computed for this note with the repository's face3d.solve.reconstruct_landmarks on face3d.synthetic data: 32 illustrative landmarks, random_subject generator (identity_sd 4, asym_sd 1, scale_sd 0.04), 26 mm-eq at 420 mm, 3000x4000 px, pitch U(-8,8) deg, prior sigma 8 mm unless noted, sigma_sym 3, sigma_mid 2, Huber 3 sigma, seed 123, 30-40 trials per row. z and NEES computed after linearised similarity alignment: e_P = P e, Sigma_P = P Sigma P, P = I - G(G^T G)^-1 G^T with G the 3N x 7 similarity tangent at the estimate; full 3N x 3N covariance captured from the Gauss-Newton inverse. Scale columns: posterior SD of the similarity-scale direction vs SD of actual scale error. Inverse-crime caveat: the generator is a smooth warp of the prior template, so real errors will be larger."
